00:32:44.120 --> 00:33:04.200
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Each week on our program, of course, we choose some theme, bring you a variety of different kinds of stories on that theme. Today's show, Say Anything, stories about what talking can accomplish and what it cannot accomplish. This show was first broadcast back in 2003. We've arrived at Act Two of our program. Act Two, The Battle of Words Versus Fear.
<v Ira Glass>这是《美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。当然，每周我们都会选择一个主题，为你带来各种各样的故事。今天的节目，“尽管说吧”，讲述谈话能成就什么以及不能成就什么。这个节目于2003年首次播出。我们来到了节目的第二章。第二章，言语与恐惧之战。

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:31.280
<v Ira Glass>Michael Bernard Loggins is in his 50s. He's developmentally disabled. He lives in San Francisco. And he says that there's certain things that he's afraid of, things that just put him on edge. And one day, he felt like he needed to write them down, just to get them out of his system. And so he started writing, numbering each fear. And it quickly got to 10, and then to 20, then to 30 and 40 and 50, till he had 138 of them on paper.
<v Ira Glass>迈克尔·伯纳德·洛金斯50多岁。他有发育障碍。他住在旧金山。他说有些事情他很害怕，有些事让他感到焦虑。有一天，他觉得需要把它们写下来，把它们排解出去。于是他开始写，为每一个恐惧编号。很快就到了10个，接着是20、30、40、50，直到纸上有了138个恐惧。

00:33:31.280 --> 00:33:57.920
<v Ira Glass>The arts program for adults where he did this, a place called Creativity Explored, published this writing as a little handwritten, xeroxed zine called, "Fears of Your Life." A few years later, Michael found that there were more fears to tame by turning them into words, and he put out a part two, a sequel titled, "Fears of Your Life, a Whole Brand New One." This one listed 45 fears. Michael gave us permission to excerpt the two books, which we do now. Actor Tom Wright is our reader.
<v Ira Glass>他完成这些作品的成人艺术项目，一个叫“创意探索”的地方，将这些文字出版成了一本手工制作、复印的小册子，名为《你生命中的恐惧》。几年后，迈克尔发现还有更多的恐惧需要通过转化为文字来驯服，他出版了第二部分，续集名为《你生命中的恐惧，一个全新的版本》。这一本列出了45个恐惧。迈克尔授权我们节选这两本书，现在我们就来读一下。演员汤姆·莱特是我们的朗读者。

00:33:57.920 --> 00:34:13.550
<v Tom Wright>Fear of hospitals and needles. Fear of school and dentists. Fear of noises and bumps in the middle of the night. Fear of doors when they slams. Fear of toys that come on by itself without anyone touching it.
<v Tom Wright>害怕医院和针头。害怕学校和牙医。害怕午夜的噪音和碰撞声。害怕关门时的巨响。害怕没人碰却会自动开启的玩具。

00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:40.990
<v Tom Wright>Fear of being caught with another woman after cheating on your wife. Fear of being in wrong places at the wrong time. Fear of dropping your soda as it hit the ground and fizz on you. Fear of tall giraffe. Fear of some birds. Fear of being different.
<v Tom Wright>害怕出轨被妻子当场抓住。害怕在错误的时间出现在错误的地点。害怕汽水掉在地上喷到自己身上。害怕长颈鹿。害怕某些鸟。害怕与众不同。

00:34:40.990 --> 00:35:12.550
<v Tom Wright>I fear that those TV people would take off my favorite cartoon, The Rugrats, off the air and wouldn't be able to watch them anymore for a long, long, long time. Please let well enough alone. Please don't take my Rugrats cartoon off the air because I love that cartoon. Let there be a possibility that life with the Rugrats stays put, means leave my Rugrats cartoon on TV, Michael said.
<v Tom Wright>我害怕那些电视节目组会把我最喜欢的动画片《淘气小兵兵》停播，那样我就不能再看它们了，很长、很长、很长的时间。请顺其自然吧。请不要停播我的《淘气小兵兵》动画片，因为我爱那部动画片。让《淘气小兵兵》的生活能持续下去吧，这意味着把我的动画片留在电视上，迈克尔说。

