<v Tom Wright>Fear if you put things that doesn't belongs in your ears and you bust the drums that's are in your ears, it liable to run you deaf, where you can't hear anything at all. You wouldn't be able to hear cars when they're coming at you. That can be a frightening and very horrible situation to happen to you if you had an occurrence in real life, especially if you comes involved in it. Can you get hit by cars if you can't hear them?
<v Tom Wright>害怕如果你把不该放的东西塞进耳朵，弄坏了耳膜，那可能会让你变聋，什么也听不见。你将听不到迎面而来的汽车声。如果现实生活中发生了这种情况，那可能是一种可怕而糟糕的情况，特别是如果你卷入其中的话。如果你听不见汽车，你会被撞到吗？

00:35:38.550 --> 00:36:12.540
<v Tom Wright>Michael is afraid and frightening and fearful when Andrea Scheer goes away for a very, very, very long, long, long, long vacational trips in order to go traveling all over the world, almost like different places and different cities and countries to visit people in her own image and own language. He afraid Andrea Scheer would come back to San Francisco, California, with all different accents and won't be able to speak Michael's English, or not be able to understand his words that he's telling her, like Merry Christmas.
<v Tom Wright>当安德烈亚·希尔为了去世界各地旅行，去不同的地方、城市和国家以她自己的形象和语言探访人们，去进行漫长的度假旅行时，迈克尔感到害怕、惊慌和忧虑。他害怕安德烈亚·希尔回到加利福尼亚的旧金山时，带着各种不同的口音，无法讲迈克尔的英语，或者听不懂他说的词，比如“圣诞快乐”。

00:36:12.540 --> 00:36:44.210
<v Tom Wright>I'm afraid and fearful that pigeons don't know right from wrong to not go out into the street. They don't have the kind of memory as we humans does to know what to do and what shall not do. They must don't know the danger of their lives are being jeopardized. And they must don't know what can definitely happen to them to humans' knowledges and sense. They land just anywhere they can find a land on surface.
<v Tom Wright>我害怕并忧虑鸽子不知道对错，不知道不去街上。它们没有我们人类那样的记忆，不知道该做什么、不该做什么。它们肯定不知道自己的生命正处于危险之中。它们肯定不知道对于人类的知识和感知来说会发生什么。它们随地降落在任何能着陆的表面上。

00:36:44.210 --> 00:37:28.380
<v Tom Wright>Fear of sharks. Fear of giant man. Fear of gorilla. Fear of Godzilla. Fear of tall woman. Fear of killer whales. Fear of dinosaurs bird. Fear of invisible man. Fear of Blob. Fear that, if I go into the library and I happens to get like seven or eight books and I happens to find a place in the library that I would get a lot of comfortable and begin reading in those seven or eight books, but one book at a time, and I start to read and somehow, my voice and mind start to get from low to high and, thinking that there weren't anyone elses reading theirs, and I look over and the people in the library, and I get fearful and I'll say, "Oops, sorry."
<v Tom Wright>害怕鲨鱼。害怕巨人。害怕大猩猩。害怕哥斯拉。害怕高个女人。害怕虎鲸。害怕恐龙鸟。害怕隐形人。害怕史莱姆。害怕如果我走进图书馆，顺手拿了七八本书，又在图书馆里找了个舒服的地方开始读这七八本书，但一次只能读一本，我开始读了，不知怎么地，我的声音和心思开始从低变高，以为没人在读他们的书，我抬头看一看图书馆里的人，我感到害怕，然后说：“喔，抱歉。”

00:37:28.380 --> 00:38:06.880
<v Tom Wright>If your friends are people that you are with and you hear them making decision about what they decided that they are going to steal expensive and very valuable merchandise out of the department stores and don't care less, you say, I am out of here. Bye bye. I'm not getting caught in your crazy schemes. I'm not your stealer partner. I'm just your friend. It's going to trouble, and it's on your head, not mine. I'm not going to participate in stealing with you, so leave me out of your crazy schemes, especially if it involve Oreo cookies and other stuff, hot stuff. Fear of me getting in trouble just as well.
<v Tom Wright>如果你的朋友是你正在相处的人，你听到他们决定要去百货商店偷昂贵且非常有价值的商品，而且毫不在意，你会说，我走人了。再见。我才不会被卷入你们疯狂的计划。我不是你们的偷窃伙伴。我只是你们的朋友。这是自找麻烦，后果由你们自己承担，不是我。我不会参与你们的偷窃，所以别把我扯进你们疯狂的计划，尤其是如果这涉及到奥利奥饼干和其他东西，那种烫手的东西。害怕我自己也惹上麻烦。

00:38:06.880 --> 00:38:33.630
<v Tom Wright>It's very scary and fearfully to be sleeping in your bed in the middle of the night whenever there's a telephone right beside the bed on you left near the door you once enter and exit out. You are sleeping. The telephone rang and scared the living life out of you in the middle of the night. Who is this calling at this hour of the night?
<v Tom Wright>在午夜时分躺在床上，当床左侧靠近出口门的地方有部电话时，那是非常可怕的。你正在睡觉。电话响了，在深夜把你吓得魂飞魄散。在这个时间点打电话来的是谁？

00:38:33.630 --> 00:38:54.630
<v Tom Wright>Fear of a blasted music on the radio, where you are not aware that the volume is turned up. Fear of rolling downhill backward. Fear of foghorn. Fear of getting hugged by somebody you don't like. There's Los Angeles fears. Fear of getting hit over the head when you carry lots of dough with you, or bucks.
<v Tom Wright>害怕收音机里的巨大音乐声，你还没意识到音量被调大了。害怕向后滚下山坡。害怕雾笛声。害怕被你不喜欢的人拥抱。洛杉矶有很多恐惧。害怕在你随身携带大量现金或钞票时被敲头。

00:38:54.630 --> 00:39:21.100
<v Tom Wright>Fear is like this. Someone like a woman that you grab a hold of her hand in going down the escalator, when of a sudden, you happens to be holding a stranger hand, not realizing that she isn't your mother is scary. Fear that if you put too much of toilet paper in the toilet bowl, it will run over and get all over the floor and on you and on someone else, too. It would leak from upstairs to the next floor below.
<v Tom Wright>恐惧是这样的。就像你拉着一个女人的手走自动扶梯时，突然之间，你握住的是一个陌生人的手，才意识到她不是你妈妈，这很可怕。害怕如果你在马桶里放太多的卫生纸，它会溢出来，弄得到处都是，弄在地上，也弄在你和别人身上。它会从楼上漏到下一层楼。

00:39:21.100 --> 00:40:00.680
<v Tom Wright>I am afraid someday I liable to get lost inside Children's Hospital if I'm not all so familiar with that place yet. It's going to take some time to get used to it. Fearfully of that great big, humongous Children's Hospital there ever would be to Michael's knowledge. Good that Michael's sister is driving him up there on Tuesday, January 15, 2002. Even though she's with him, she can easily get lost, too. Bad situation to tangled up in, especially if you that person has an appointment at 10:45 AM in the morning. Michael Bernard Loggins does.
<v Tom Wright>我担心有一天我可能会在儿童医院迷路，如果我还不太熟悉那个地方的话。得花点时间适应它。对迈克尔所知的有史以来最大、最庞大的儿童医院感到恐惧。迈克尔的姐姐在2002年1月15日星期二开车带他去那里，这很好。即使她和他在一起，她也很容易迷路。陷入这种糟糕的情况中，尤其是如果那个人在上午10点45分有预约。迈克尔·伯纳德·洛金斯就有。

