<v Tom Wright>It would be very fearful if I reached up on top shelf trying to reach for a nice thicker-covered dictionary book and not ask for help from someone and the books come off the shelf and make lots of noises and the people gets angry at me and don't understand that I had want help, but I were afraid to ask for it. And they'd be a jerk or a creep, as Hope tells me. And people say that I'll have to pay for the shelf, and I get in lots of trouble behind it, says Michael.
<v Tom Wright>如果我伸手去够顶架上的那本厚皮字典，而没有向别人求助，书架上的书掉下来发出巨大的噪音，人们对我生气，却不理解我其实想要帮助，只是害怕去要求，那会非常令人恐惧。他们会像“希望”告诉我的那样，是个混蛋或讨厌鬼。人们说我必须赔偿书架，我会被卷入很多麻烦，迈克尔说。

00:41:00.890 --> 00:41:36.790
<v Tom Wright>Fear of being with a friend that you have recently met start to take you places with him and you doesn't know him all that well. You didn't know that he were going to bring you fear and lots of trouble your way. Someone you doesn't know all that well starts to carry you in the store to buy you and him something to eat and drink, and all of the sudden, something very fishy starts to happen. Like for instance, your friend that you are with could be up to trouble and whoever with him could be heading in for trouble, as well, especially if a friend of yours could be bringing you trouble by stealing a big package of Oreo cookie.
<v Tom Wright>害怕与刚认识的朋友在一起，他开始带你去一些地方，而你对他并不了解。你不知道他会给你带来恐惧和很多麻烦。一个你并不了解的人开始带你去商店给你和他也买点吃喝的，突然之间，一些非常可疑的事情开始发生。比如，你同行的朋友可能在惹麻烦，而和他在一起的任何人也可能惹上麻烦，尤其是如果你的朋友通过偷一大包奥利奥饼干来给你带来麻烦的话。

00:41:36.790 --> 00:42:27.860
<v Tom Wright>People are fearful of me, which I wonder, is they think I'm all that terrible? Or I'm thinking that they think I'm not human at all, because when they sit next to me, then they get back up and move away from me. I may be a stranger, but that doesn't make me a created monster or something like that. People aren't humans. They act like ignorance dogs with their tail in back of their legs or in between their middle bodies their legs. They don't think whose feeling they hurt at all. They just do it, no consideration for whatsoever. People don't think about how they hurt my feelings or don't give a hoot. They don't give a crap.
<v Tom Wright>人们对我感到恐惧，我很好奇，他们认为我真有那么糟糕吗？或者我想他们认为我根本不是人类，因为当他们坐在我旁边时，他们会起身走开。我可能是一个陌生人，但这并不会让我变成创造出来的怪物之类的东西。人们不是人类。他们表现得像无知的狗，尾巴夹在腿中间或后腿之间。他们根本不在乎自己伤害了谁的感情。他们就这样做了，完全不顾他人。人们不考虑他们如何伤害我的感情，也不在乎。他们根本不在乎。

00:42:27.860 --> 00:43:06.070
<v Tom Wright>Fear of you never knowing you were going to lose your mother is very sad and scary experience you have to face and learn from. And you wonder why she has to die. I love her. And I had loved her once while she were alive, especially if she was the mother that raised you and the others through birth. And you only wish that you could have done all you can to help save her life. There going to be a worse times and hard times for Michael Bernard Loggins and his sisters and brothers, too, especially when Mother's Day comes. Afraid this is the last thing that ever occur to me.
<v Tom Wright>害怕你永远不知道自己会失去母亲，这是一种你必须面对并从中学习的非常悲伤和可怕的经历。你会纳闷为什么她不得不死。我爱她。当她还活着的时候，我爱过她，尤其是如果她是那个把你和其他人抚养长大的母亲。你只希望你能尽你所能去救她的命。对迈克尔·伯纳德·洛金斯和他的姐妹兄弟们来说，会有更糟的时期和艰难时刻，尤其是在母亲节的时候。害怕这是最后一件发生在我身上的事情。

